    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0229" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 639.003/32.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s No. 53 of
                    June 15, and to my No. 64 of July 8, I have the honor to inclose you herewith
                    copies and translations of the reply of the minister for foreign affairs to my
                    note forwarding a memorandum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d165-f1"/> reiterating and
                    reaffirming the views of the Government of the United States as to the proper
                    interpretation of the convention of February 8, 1907, in regard to the law of
                    the Dominican Republic providing for the imposition of a stamp tax on foreign
                    and domestic letters of exchange, etc., and a resolution of the Dominican
                    Congress putting into operation a municipal surtax upon articles of import
                    levied by the commune of Santo Domingo.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William W.
                    Russell.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d165-a1.xml" xpointer="d165-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
